### BundleIt Bundles Service - REST API Test Cases
### This file contains ready-to-run HTTP requests for the Bundles context
### Use with VS Code REST Client or similar HTTP client

@BaseUrl = http://localhost:5284/api/bundles
@DemoArtistId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@CoopArtistId = 99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999
@ActiveBundleId = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@ArchivedBundleId = 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333

### ============================================================================
### 1. GET - Retrieve all seeded bundles (200 OK)
### Expected: Returns array of 2 bundles (active published + archived)
### ============================================================================
GET {{BaseUrl}}
Accept: application/json

###

### ============================================================================
### 2. GET - Retrieve the active published bundle (200 OK)
### Expected: Returns bundle with status "Published", 2 items, 1 co-op artist
### ============================================================================
GET {{BaseUrl}}/{{ActiveBundleId}}
Accept: application/json

###

### ============================================================================
### 3. GET - Retrieve the archived bundle (200 OK)
### Expected: Returns bundle with status "Archived", 1 item, no co-op artists
### ============================================================================
GET {{BaseUrl}}/{{ArchivedBundleId}}
Accept: application/json

###

### ============================================================================
### 4. POST - Create a new bundle (201 Created)
### Creates a new Personal License bundle with initial pricing
### Expected: 201 Created with Location header and new bundle data
### ============================================================================
POST {{BaseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "primaryArtistId": "{{DemoArtistId}}",
  "title": "Digital Illustration 101 Bundle",
  "packLicenseType": "Personal",
  "personalPrice": 19.99,
  "currency": "USD",
  "commercialPrice": null,
  "description": "Complete beginner's digital illustration course with 500+ brushes and textures for personal use only."
}

###

### ============================================================================
### 5. POST - Add an item to the active bundle (200 OK)
### Valid state transition: Adding item to existing published bundle
### Expected: 200 OK with updated bundle containing new item
### ============================================================================
POST {{BaseUrl}}/{{ActiveBundleId}}/items
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "itemId": "44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444",
  "name": "Advanced Digital Painting Techniques",
  "licenseType": "Commercial",
  "description": "Video tutorials and reference materials for professional digital painters",
  "fileFormat": "ZIP",
  "fileSizeBytes": 2500000000
}

###

### ============================================================================
### 6. POST - Attempt to add item to archived bundle (422 Unprocessable Entity)
### Business rule violation: Cannot add items to archived bundles (Invariant #10)
### Expected: 422 with error code "BundleArchived"
### ============================================================================
POST {{BaseUrl}}/{{ArchivedBundleId}}/items
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "itemId": "55555555-5555-5555-5555-555555555555",
  "name": "This Should Fail",
  "licenseType": "Personal",
  "description": "Cannot add items to archived bundle - should return 422",
  "fileFormat": "ZIP",
  "fileSizeBytes": 50000000
}

###

### ============================================================================
### 7. POST - Create empty bundle for publishing test (201 Created)
### Creates a draft bundle with no items
### Expected: 201 Created with status "Draft"
### ============================================================================
POST {{BaseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "primaryArtistId": "{{DemoArtistId}}",
  "title": "Empty Bundle For Testing",
  "packLicenseType": "Commercial",
  "personalPrice": 50.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "commercialPrice": 100.00,
  "description": "This bundle intentionally has no items to test publishing invariant"
}

###

### ============================================================================
### 8. POST - Attempt to publish empty bundle (422 Unprocessable Entity)
### Business rule violation: Bundle must contain at least 1 item (Invariant #11)
### Expected: 422 with error code "EmptyBundle"
### Note: Uncomment this after creating the empty bundle in step 7, 
### then replace {emptyBundleId} with the ID returned from step 7
### ============================================================================
# POST {{BaseUrl}}/{emptyBundleId}/publish
# Accept: application/json

###

### ============================================================================
### 9. POST - Publish the active bundle (200 OK)
### Valid state transition: Publish draft bundle with items
### Note: If the bundle is already published, this will not change state but return 200
### Expected: 200 OK with updated bundle status "Published"
### ============================================================================
# POST {{BaseUrl}}/{{ActiveBundleId}}/publish
# Accept: application/json

###

### ============================================================================
### 10. POST - Archive the active bundle (200 OK)
### Valid state transition: Archive published bundle
### Expected: 200 OK with updated bundle status "Archived"
### Note: After archiving, the bundle cannot accept new items (see step 6)
### ============================================================================
# POST {{BaseUrl}}/{{ActiveBundleId}}/archive
# Accept: application/json

###

### ============================================================================
### 11. DELETE - Delete the active bundle (204 No Content)
### Removes the bundle and all associated items via cascading delete
### Expected: 204 No Content (no response body)
### Note: Uncomment after testing other operations
### ============================================================================
# DELETE {{BaseUrl}}/{{ActiveBundleId}}
# Accept: application/json

###

### ============================================================================
### 12. GET - Attempt to retrieve deleted bundle (404 Not Found)
### Expected: 404 Not Found
### Note: Run this after step 11 to verify deletion
### ============================================================================
# GET {{BaseUrl}}/{{ActiveBundleId}}
# Accept: application/json

###

### ============================================================================
### ERROR CASES & INVARIANTS TESTED
### ============================================================================
### ? Invariant #10: Archived bundle cannot accept new items ? 422 (step 6)
### ? Invariant #11: Empty bundle cannot be published ? 422 (step 8)
### ? Invariant #12: Commercial price >= Personal price (enforced in Bundle constructor)
### ? Invariant #13: License type mismatch between bundle and items (enforced in AddItem)
### ? Not Found: Requesting non-existent bundle ? 404
### ? Created: Creating new bundle ? 201 with Location header
### ? Success: State transitions (publish, archive) ? 200 OK
### ? No Content: Deleting resource ? 204 No Content

###

### ============================================================================
### STEP-BY-STEP WORKFLOW INSTRUCTIONS
### ============================================================================
### 1. Start the application:
###    cd src/Services/Bundles/EShopService.Bundles.Presentation
###    dotnet run
### 
### 2. Run request #1 (GET all) - See the 2 seeded bundles
### 3. Run request #2 (GET active bundle) - Inspect Published bundle with 2 items
### 4. Run request #3 (GET archived bundle) - Inspect Archived bundle
### 5. Run request #4 (POST create) - Create new bundle, copy the BundleId from response
### 6. Run request #5 (POST add item) - Add item to active published bundle
### 7. Run request #6 (POST add to archived) - Should get 422 error (business rule)
### 8. Run request #7 (POST create empty) - Create empty bundle, copy BundleId
### 9. Uncomment/modify request #8, replace {emptyBundleId} - Should get 422 error
### 10. Uncomment request #9 - Publish the active bundle
### 11. Uncomment request #10 - Archive the active bundle
### 12. Uncomment/modify request #11 - Delete with an unused bundle ID
### 13. Uncomment/modify request #12 - Try to GET deleted bundle ? 404
###
